# Performance

## Default strategy

Prefer HTML over JavaScript.
Prefer server-rendered content over client-side rendering.
Prefer local/simple computation over large browser libraries.

## Hydration

Every React island must justify its hydration.
Use the least aggressive Astro hydration directive that satisfies the UX.

Do not hydrate static content.

## JavaScript

Avoid adding libraries for tasks that can be handled with:
- native browser APIs
- Astro
- TypeScript
- small utilities

Avoid duplicated client-side data-fetching layers.

## Images

Optimize image dimensions and delivery.
Set width/height or equivalent layout reservation.
Lazy-load below-the-fold images where appropriate.
Do not lazy-load the primary hero image when it harms LCP.

## Fonts

Use a restrained font stack.
Avoid loading many font files or unnecessary weights.

Prevent layout shifts caused by font loading.

## Data fetching

Fetch only the content required for the page.
Avoid making multiple sequential requests for content that can be fetched together.

## Caching

Use appropriate caching/revalidation for content that changes less frequently.
Do not introduce complex caching infrastructure without a real need.

## Core Web Vitals mindset

Protect:
- LCP
- CLS
- INP

Visual sophistication must not come at the cost of usability or loading performance.
